+			// -- a scripted STEP LIST, after the load (Kyoti local) ----------
+			// Why: a diagnostic is rarely ONE call.  Route A's Python drivers
+			// interleave `run(until=main spin)`, `call_as_main`, pokes and
+			// reads dozens of times per test, and paid route A's whole
+			// per-instruction tax to do it.  This runs the same sequence
+			// natively, in one process, on one load.
+			//
+			//   ptr  NAME=ADDR        bind NAME to the 32-bit word AT ADDR
+			//   set  NAME=VALUE       bind NAME to a literal
+			//   spin                  run to main's spin (what callAsMain needs)
+			//   call TARGET[,ARG..]   callAsMain; prints d0
+			//   poke ADDR=HEXBYTES    write those bytes (even length, no 0x)
+			//   copy DST=SRC,LEN      guest-to-guest memcpy (seed an arena entry
+			//                         from another without a round trip to the host)
+			//   peek ADDR,LEN         print LEN bytes as hex
+			//   echo TEXT             a label, passed through
+			//
